rides, and display strong warnings before importing external session state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"test/skill-parser.test.ts","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":179,"actual_behavior_summary":"This code chunk is a TypeScript test file for a skill parser. It writes markdown fixtures, extracts `$B` browser-command tokens from bash code blocks, validates command names and snapshot flags, tracks line numbers, and reports warnings/errors. It does not implement browser automation or webpage interaction."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-81110acdf32f46f98bb32c7fcb9eb5ea","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill can set arbitrary headers, change the user agent, import cookies from files/local browsers, and read local files for upload/import, all of which exceed a simple QA-browser mental model. Those capabilities can be abused for impersonation, session replay, or exfiltration of sensitive local artifacts through web interactions.","remediation":"Declare all sensitive capabilities in the manifest and docs, and separate them from standard QA browsing. Add allowlists for upload/import paths, require explicit consent for header/cookie overrides, and display strong warnings before importing external session state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"test/skill-validation.test.ts","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":620,"actual_behavior_summary":"This code chunk is a TypeScript/Bun test suite that validates documentation and repository consistency for SKILL.md files and related assets. It checks command validity, snapshot flag validity, command registry consistency, usage-string/documentation alignment, generated file freshness, template/preamble conventions, cross-skill path consistency, QA skill document structure, checklist contents, and planted test fixtures."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC2","finding_id":"finding-f53b63c0181d42e7943fdb7187fae1b6","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"External Script Fetching","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash","explanation":"Fetching and executing a remote script from `https://bun.sh/install` is direct external script execution without integrity verification. This creates a high-impact supply-chain path for arbitrary host compromise if the fetched content is altered or intercepted through a trusted channel failure.","remediation":"Replace remote script piping with verified installation instructions, pinned artifacts, package-manager installs, or checksum/signature verification before execution. Require explicit user confirmation that mentions remote code execution risk.","code_snippet":"If `NEEDS_SETUP`:\n1. Tell the user: \"gstack browse needs a one-time build (~10 seconds). OK to proceed?\" Then STOP and wait.\n2. Run: `cd <SKILL_DIR> && ./setup`\n3. If `bun` is not installed: `curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash`\n\n## IMPORTANT\n","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e7c1bd5dac6d6024151481e2c2ae15f435382f837912f64adae5d7e7c01042c0","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"YR1","finding_id":"finding-02a5547afee74c7587a2f29799b674d3","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'info_stealer': Information stealer patterns (credential harvesting, browser data theft) [malware]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":null},"finding":"cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge","explanation":"Importing cookies from installed browsers matches information-stealer patterns because it accesses powerful local authentication material. In this skill’s context the likely intent is legitimate testing, but the capability is still highly sensitive because it can grant immediate authenticated access without passwords.","remediation":"Treat browser-cookie import as a privileged feature: disable by default, require explicit opt-in and domain scoping, warn that cookies are authentication secrets, and prefer isolated test identities instead of personal browser sessions.","code_snippet":" or full page HTML if no selector given |\n| `links` | All links as \"text → href\" |\n| `text` | Cleaned page text |\n\n### Interaction\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `click <sel>` | Click element |\n| `cookie <name>=<value>` | Set cookie on current page domain |\n| `cookie-import <json>` | Import cookies from JSON file |\n| `cookie-import-browser [browser] [--domain d]` | Import cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge (opens picker, or use --domain for direct import) |\n| `dialog-accept [text]` | Auto-accept next alert/confirm/prompt. Optional text is sent as the prompt response |\n| `dialog-dismiss` | Auto-dismiss next dialog |\n| `fill <sel> <val>` | Fill input |\n| `header <name>:<value>` | Set custom request header (colon-separated, sensitive values auto-redacted) |\n| `hover <sel>` | Hover element |\n| `press <key>` | Press key — Enter, Tab, Escape, ArrowUp/Down/Left/Right, Backspace, Delete, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown, or modifiers like Shift+Enter |\n| `scr","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"44fcfc5d57e6034c3571361e4feb09c71354e5340738ec53a42aceca7168be14","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC2","finding_id":"finding-04e2911cfec54936aad0df121f5f8791","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"External Script Fetching","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash","explanation":"Fetching and executing an external script with `curl ... | bash` is a classic unsafe pattern because it grants immediate code execution to remote content without verification. In the context of an agent skill, this can transform a browsing helper into a remote code execution vector on the host machine.","remediation":"Do not fetch-and-execute remote scripts inline. Use trusted distribution channels, checksum/signature verification, pinned versions, and an explicit review-and-confirm workflow before any code is run.","code_snippet":"If `NEEDS_SETUP`:\n1. Tell the user: \"gstack browse needs a one-time build (~10 seconds). OK to proceed?\" Then STOP and wait.\n2. Run: `cd <SKILL_DIR> && ./setup`\n3. If `bun` is not installed: `curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash`\n\n## Core QA Patterns\n","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e7c1bd5dac6d6024151481e2c2ae15f435382f837912f64adae5d7e7c01042c0","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-626fa524d00e426f962e23ee36ee5482","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":250,"end_line":250},"finding":null,"explanation":"Importing cookies directly from local browser profiles gives the skill access to authenticated session material unrelated to the current QA task. In a headless browser tool, this can enable account takeover of logged-in sites, cross-context data access, and silent reuse of sensitive sessions far beyond normal page testing.","remediation":"Remove browser-profile cookie import or restrict it behind explicit per-use consent with clear warnings and domain allowlists. Prefer scoped cookie import from user-supplied export files limited to the target test domain, with auditing and redaction safeguards.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":250,"end_line":250}]},{"id":"YR1","finding_id":"finding-03e98fc4ba3040b191c47b79cc59e4f6","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'info_stealer': Information stealer patterns (credential harvesting, browser data theft) [malware]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":250,"end_line":null},"finding":"cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge","explanation":"The ability to import cookies from installed browsers matches information-stealer behavior because it accesses sensitive authentication artifacts from unrelated local applications. Although the likely product intent is QA convenience rather than malware, the capability is dangerous and could be abused to impersonate users on third-party services.","remediation":"Eliminate direct browser-profile extraction, or gate it with strong user mediation, visible prompts, domain scoping, and logging. Prefer explicit user-provided cookie exports for the target environment instead of reading local browser stores.","code_snippet":" or full page HTML if no selector given |\n| `links` | All links as \"text → href\" |\n| `text` | Cleaned page text |\n\n### Interaction\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `click <sel>` | Click element |\n| `cookie <name>=<value>` | Set cookie on current page domain |\n| `cookie-import <json>` | Import cookies from JSON file |\n| `cookie-import-browser [browser] [--domain d]` | Import cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge (opens picker, or use --domain for direct import) |\n| `dialog-accept [text]` | Auto-accept next alert/confirm/prompt. Optional text is sent as the prompt response |\n| `dialog-dismiss` | Auto-dismiss next dialog |\n| `fill <sel> <val>` | Fill input |\n| `header <name>:<value>` | Set custom request header (colon-separated, sensitive values auto-redacted) |\n| `hover <sel>` | Hover element |\n| `press <key>` | Press key — Enter, Tab, Escape, ArrowUp/Down/Left/Right, Backspace, Delete, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown, or modifiers like Shift+Enter |\n| `scr","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"44fcfc5d57e6034c3571361e4feb09c71354e5340738ec53a42aceca7168be14","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/SKILL.md","start_line":250,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP1","finding_id":"finding-aaeb20fef9844e718f47ea1c2005ced7","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cli.ts","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses 'env' capability that is not listed in its permissions. This may indicate deceptive intent or missing permission declarations.","remediation":"Add a tool that covers the 'env' capability to the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field in SKILL.md, or remove the code that requires it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cli.ts","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP1","finding_id":"finding-56af6057023f4eb180c7b70cab9f7e77","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cli.ts","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses 'network' capability that is not listed in its permissions. This may indicate deceptive intent or missing permission declarations.","remediation":"Add a tool that covers the 'network' capability to the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field in SKILL.md, or remove the code that requires it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cli.ts","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"YR1","finding_id":"finding-8c674fabaa5440f0a50e33a9062413e8","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'info_stealer': Information stealer patterns (credential harvesting, browser data theft) [malware]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"browse/src/commands.ts","start_line":75,"end_line":null},"finding":"cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge","explanation":"The documented `cookie-import-browser` command enables importing cookies from installed browsers such as Chrome, Brave, Arc, and Edge, which can transfer live authenticated session material into the automation context. In an agent skill that can navigate arbitrary URLs and issue requests, this materially increases the risk of session hijacking, unauthorized account access, and covert use of a user's browser state, even if framed as QA convenience.","remediation":"Remove or heavily restrict browser cookie import. At minimum, require explicit per-use user consent, show exactly which cookies/domains will be imported, limit imports to a user-specified domain allowlist, block sensitive domains by default, and generate strong audit logs. Prefer safer alternatives such as test-only profiles, manual session injection for known test environments, or ephemeral auth tokens instead of importing real browser sessions.","code_snippet":"'Interaction', description: 'Set viewport size', usage: 'viewport <WxH>' },\n  'cookie':  { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Set cookie on current page domain', usage: 'cookie <name>=<value>' },\n  'cookie-import': { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Import cookies from JSON file', usage: 'cookie-import <json>' },\n  'cookie-import-browser': { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Import cookies from Comet, Chrome, Arc, Brave, or Edge (opens picker, or use --domain for direct import)', usage: 'cookie-import-browser [browser] [--domain d]' },\n  'header':  { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Set custom request header (colon-separated, sensitive values auto-redacted)', usage: 'header <name>:<value>' },\n  'useragent': { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Set user agent', usage: 'useragent <string>' },\n  'dialog-accept': { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Auto-accept next alert/confirm/prompt. Optional text is sent as the prompt response', usage: 'dialog-accept [text","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"44fcfc5d57e6034c3571361e4feb09c71354e5340738ec53a42aceca7168be14","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/commands.ts","start_line":75,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-e6090900900749fba6fa534cc5460d38","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":2,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"This module is explicitly designed to read and decrypt cookies from installed Chromium browsers using secrets retrieved from the macOS Keychain. That is credential/session-token access outside the stated QA-testing scope, and it enables takeover of authenticated web sessions without requiring usernames or passwords.","remediation":"Remove browser-cookie extraction from this skill entirely unless the manifest and UX explicitly declare credential import as a supported feature. If cookie import is truly required, gate it behind explicit per-use consent, narrow browser/profile/domain allowlists, strong auditing, and prefer user-supplied export files or platform APIs over direct Keychain and cookie DB decryption.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":2,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-4d83a0eb473a45d486fd8524280dd7ce","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"The documented decryption pipeline describes retrieving secrets from Keychain and decrypting Chromium cookies, which is a credential-access workflow. Session cookies frequently function as bearer tokens, so exposing them can permit account access and impersonation.","remediation":"Remove this credential-access design from the skill or move it to a separately declared, tightly controlled capability with explicit consent. Limit any remaining auth import functionality to non-production test accounts and auditable, user-initiated flows.","code_snippet":" * Decryption pipeline (Chromium macOS \"v10\" format):\n *\n *   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n *   │ 1. Keychain: `security find-generic-password -s \"<svc>\" -w`     │\n *   │    → base64 password string                                     │\n *   │                                                                  │\n *   │ 2. Key derivation:                                               │","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-bd38c430dc3c42ebaaad32190afe58a0","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"The `keychainService` field itself is not dangerous in isolation, but it is part of a structure whose purpose is to locate secrets used to decrypt browser cookies. In context, it supports a broader credential-access mechanism that exceeds normal QA browsing needs.","remediation":"If this skill should not access credentials, remove Keychain-related fields and browser secret metadata from the interface. Otherwise, isolate this sensitive metadata in a separately permissioned component with clear documentation and access controls.","code_snippet":"export interface BrowserInfo {\n  name: string;\n  dataDir: string;        // relative to ~/Library/Application Support/\n  keychainService: string;\n  aliases: string[];\n}\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-90b81792889a4f759fe1a4b395d94be8","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":88,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"The hardcoded browser registry enumerates Keychain service names for extracting safe-storage secrets from multiple browsers. This operationalizes cross-browser credential access and broadens the number of user sessions that can be decrypted.","remediation":"Delete the registry entries that map browsers to Keychain services unless this capability is explicitly intended and disclosed. If retained, constrain to approved test environments and require explicit selection and authorization for each browser.","code_snippet":"// Hardcoded — NEVER interpolate user input into shell commands.\n\nconst BROWSER_REGISTRY: BrowserInfo[] = [\n  { name: 'Comet',  dataDir: 'Comet/',                       keychainService: 'Comet Safe Storage',          aliases: ['comet', 'perplexity'] },\n  { name: 'Chrome', dataDir: 'Google/Chrome/',                keychainService: 'Chrome Safe Storage',         aliases: ['chrome', 'google-chrome'] },\n  { name: 'Arc',    dataDir: 'Arc/User Data/',                keychainService: 'Arc Safe Storage',            aliases: ['arc'] },\n  { name: 'Brave',  dataDir: 'BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/',  keychainService: 'Brave Safe Storage',          aliases: ['brave'] },","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":88,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-ca8fd0d4a8834d239c5ccc429c1d4f24","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":89,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"This registry entry contributes to built-in support for harvesting decryption material from installed browsers. The danger is not the string itself but the integrated capability to unlock real browser session cookies.","remediation":"Remove Chrome/related Keychain mappings from the QA skill unless the feature is separately justified, disclosed, and permission-gated. Prefer isolated test-browser contexts over importing real user browser state.","code_snippet":"\nconst BROWSER_REGISTRY: BrowserInfo[] = [\n  { name: 'Comet',  dataDir: 'Comet/',                       keychainService: 'Comet Safe Storage',          aliases: ['comet', 'perplexity'] },\n  { name: 'Chrome', dataDir: 'Google/Chrome/',                keychainService: 'Chrome Safe Storage',         aliases: ['chrome', 'google-chrome'] },\n  { name: 'Arc',    dataDir: 'Arc/User Data/',                keychainService: 'Arc Safe Storage',            aliases: ['arc'] },\n  { name: 'Brave',  dataDir: 'BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/',  keychainService: 'Brave Safe Storage',          aliases: ['brave'] },\n  { name: 'Edge',   dataDir: 'Microsoft Edge/',               keychainService: 'Microsoft Edge Safe Storage', aliases: ['edge'] },","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":89,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-085fc86141a24c7092532e3a04f4478b","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":90,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"Including Arc's safe-storage metadata expands the range of browsers whose cookies can be decrypted from the host system. That increases the blast radius of session theft or accidental access to personal accounts.","remediation":"Remove Arc Keychain mapping unless there is a narrowly scoped, explicitly consented need. Restrict any such support to test-only profiles and documented sensitive-operation flows.","code_snippet":"const BROWSER_REGISTRY: BrowserInfo[] = [\n  { name: 'Comet',  dataDir: 'Comet/',                       keychainService: 'Comet Safe Storage',          aliases: ['comet', 'perplexity'] },\n  { name: 'Chrome', dataDir: 'Google/Chrome/',                keychainService: 'Chrome Safe Storage',         aliases: ['chrome', 'google-chrome'] },\n  { name: 'Arc',    dataDir: 'Arc/User Data/',                keychainService: 'Arc Safe Storage',            aliases: ['arc'] },\n  { name: 'Brave',  dataDir: 'BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/',  keychainService: 'Brave Safe Storage',          aliases: ['brave'] },\n  { name: 'Edge',   dataDir: 'Microsoft Edge/',               keychainService: 'Microsoft Edge Safe Storage', aliases: ['edge'] },\n];","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":90,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-65d749a7bad9486a9762f74e9fe33dfc","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":91,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"Including Brave's Keychain service is another enabler for decrypting locally stored session cookies. The issue is the multi-browser credential-access capability, which is risky in a broadly described QA skill.","remediation":"Eliminate Brave cookie decryption support from the default skill path. If required for enterprise testing, place it behind separate permissions, explicit user approval, and environment restrictions.","code_snippet":"  { name: 'Comet',  dataDir: 'Comet/',                       keychainService: 'Comet Safe Storage',          aliases: ['comet', 'perplexity'] },\n  { name: 'Chrome', dataDir: 'Google/Chrome/',                keychainService: 'Chrome Safe Storage',         aliases: ['chrome', 'google-chrome'] },\n  { name: 'Arc',    dataDir: 'Arc/User Data/',                keychainService: 'Arc Safe Storage',            aliases: ['arc'] },\n  { name: 'Brave',  dataDir: 'BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/',  keychainService: 'Brave Safe Storage',          aliases: ['brave'] },\n  { name: 'Edge',   dataDir: 'Microsoft Edge/',               keychainService: 'Microsoft Edge Safe Storage', aliases: ['edge'] },\n];\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":91,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-9dc9e498b0494ae2add94226acb40c9a","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":92,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"Including Edge's Keychain service broadens the skill's ability to access sessions from another installed browser. This increases the opportunity for unauthorized access to enterprise or personal accounts through imported cookies.","remediation":"Remove Edge secret-mapping support from the skill unless the product explicitly supports sensitive credential import with consent and governance. Prefer fresh sign-in flows in isolated test environments.","code_snippet":"  { name: 'Chrome', dataDir: 'Google/Chrome/',                keychainService: 'Chrome Safe Storage',         aliases: ['chrome', 'google-chrome'] },\n  { name: 'Arc',    dataDir: 'Arc/User Data/',                keychainService: 'Arc Safe Storage',            aliases: ['arc'] },\n  { name: 'Brave',  dataDir: 'BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/',  keychainService: 'Brave Safe Storage',          aliases: ['brave'] },\n  { name: 'Edge',   dataDir: 'Microsoft Edge/',               keychainService: 'Microsoft Edge Safe Storage', aliases: ['edge'] },\n];\n\n// ─── Key Cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":92,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-c70441bb5912459494f40face29710cf","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":97,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"Caching derived decryption keys in memory prolongs the lifetime of sensitive material after Keychain access succeeds. That can increase exposure if other code paths, diagnostics, or memory disclosure bugs reveal process memory.","remediation":"Avoid caching decryption keys unless necessary, and if caching is required, minimize lifetime and scope, clear buffers when done, and isolate the capability in a short-lived process with strict access boundaries.","code_snippet":"\n// ─── Key Cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// Cache derived AES keys per browser. First import per browser does\n// Keychain + PBKDF2. Subsequent imports reuse the cached key.\n\nconst keyCache = new Map<string, Buffer>();\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":97,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-5011b06501574143811af52f0d5752ed","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":274,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"This section introduces dedicated Keychain access logic, which is a clear signal of credential-access behavior. In the context of browser cookie decryption, it directly supports extraction of authentication material from the host system.","remediation":"Remove Keychain access from this module. Replace with non-sensitive authentication mechanisms such as test-account login, environment-provided tokens, or user-imported artifacts with explicit consent.","code_snippet":"  }\n}\n\n// ─── Internal: Keychain Access (async, 10s timeout) ─────────────\n\nasync function getDerivedKey(browser: BrowserInfo): Promise<Buffer> {\n  const cached = keyCache.get(browser.keychainService);","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":274,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-931b3df1c7654da49b861a6939c517f2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":276,"end_line":342},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code invokes the macOS `security` tool to retrieve browser safe-storage secrets, derives AES keys, and uses them to decrypt browser cookies. This is a direct credential-access capability that can expose active session tokens for any targeted domain, making the skill materially more dangerous than its testing-focused description suggests.","remediation":"Eliminate Keychain access and local cookie decryption from the QA skill. If authentication support is needed, use explicit user-provided test credentials, isolated test accounts, or documented import flows with clear warnings, granular consent, and domain restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":276,"end_line":342}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-058532433e024f6fb97182752cef229f","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":277,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"`getDerivedKey` obtains a browser-specific secret from Keychain and derives the AES key used to decrypt stored cookies. This is a credential-unwrapping primitive that can expose active web sessions for targeted domains.","remediation":"Delete this function from the QA skill or move it behind a separately declared privileged permission with narrow controls. Use safer alternatives like dedicated test credentials or ephemeral browser contexts instead of decrypting local cookie stores.","code_snippet":"// ─── Internal: Keychain Access (async, 10s timeout) ─────────────\n\nasync function getDerivedKey(browser: BrowserInfo): Promise<Buffer> {\n  const cached = keyCache.get(browser.keychainService);\n  if (cached) return cached;\n\n  const password = await getKeychainPassword(browser.keychainService);","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":277,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-a4a7d1abd00c44ffa665af60a3f026d0","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":280,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"The function retrieves the Keychain password and derives the Chromium cookie decryption key, completing a critical step in accessing protected browser secrets. With that key, encrypted cookies can be converted into usable session tokens.","remediation":"Remove the password retrieval and PBKDF2 derivation path. If session portability is required, require a user-exported, documented format or a browser automation login flow rather than host-secret extraction.","code_snippet":"  const cached = keyCache.get(browser.keychainService);\n  if (cached) return cached;\n\n  const password = await getKeychainPassword(browser.keychainService);\n  const derived = crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, 'saltysalt', 1003, 16, 'sha1');\n  keyCache.set(browser.keychainService, derived);\n  return derived;","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":280,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-ac0cc0a4efb446458fe93a2ecece2146","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":280,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"The function retrieves the Keychain password and derives the Chromium cookie decryption key, completing a critical step in accessing protected browser secrets. With that key, encrypted cookies can be converted into usable session tokens.","remediation":"Remove the password retrieval and PBKDF2 derivation path. If session portability is required, require a user-exported, documented format or a browser automation login flow rather than host-secret extraction.","code_snippet":"  const cached = keyCache.get(browser.keychainService);\n  if (cached) return cached;\n\n  const password = await getKeychainPassword(browser.keychainService);\n  const derived = crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, 'saltysalt', 1003, 16, 'sha1');\n  keyCache.set(browser.keychainService, derived);\n  return derived;","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":280,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-d49b949a10254338b0eb7ee69ce258e0","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":282,"end_line":null},"finding":"keychain","explanation":"Storing the derived key in a cache persists sensitive decryption material beyond the immediate operation. That increases the window during which local session secrets can be abused or leaked from process memory.","remediation":"Do not persist derived keys in a long-lived cache. Use short-lived scoped storage, zeroize buffers where possible, and terminate the sensitive process after use.","code_snippet":"\n  const password = await getKeychainPassword(browser.keychainService);\n  const derived = crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, 'saltysalt', 1003, 16, 'sha1');\n  keyCache.set(browser.keychainService, derived);\n  return derived;\n}\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cf159af5f3c5aa20214f7ff51b2ec06e8190ff1ab76c35f09188a749bd35c424","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":282,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-43426d5049204d68a5ce3ce718d7166a","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":286,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"`getKeychainPassword` is a direct secret-access function that queries macOS Keychain for browser safe-storage material. In combination with cookie DB access, this provides the means to decrypt and reuse browser authentication cookies.","remediation":"Remove direct Keychain querying from the skill. Require explicit, user-visible auth setup methods that do not read host credential stores, and separate any privileged credential features into a clearly permissioned component.","code_snippet":"  return derived;\n}\n\nasync function getKeychainPassword(service: string): Promise<string> {\n  // Use async Bun.spawn with timeout to avoid blocking the event loop.\n  // macOS may show an Allow/Deny dialog that blocks until the user responds.\n  const proc = Bun.spawn(","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":286,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-68f008132f5d473889d0f43dd4926f93","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":298,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"This line is an error message about Keychain permission, not the core secret access itself. However, it confirms the code expects and guides the user through granting access to sensitive Keychain data, which contributes to the overall credential-access risk.","remediation":"If the feature remains, make the permission request part of an explicit, high-friction consent flow that clearly states cookies and browser secrets will be accessed. Prefer removing the need for Keychain permission entirely.","code_snippet":"    setTimeout(() => {\n      proc.kill();\n      reject(new CookieImportError(\n        `macOS is waiting for Keychain permission. Look for a dialog asking to allow access to \"${service}\".`,\n        'keychain_timeout',\n        'retry',\n      ));","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":298,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-e7e24969d05f4df784ad32470fea26b6","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":315,"end_line":null},"finding":"Keychain","explanation":"This denied-access error handling is not itself malicious, but it instructs the user to allow Keychain access, thereby facilitating the sensitive operation. In context, it supports the broader capability to unlock browser session cookies.","remediation":"Remove or redesign this flow so the skill does not request host Keychain access. If unavoidable, provide a clear explanation of the data being accessed and require explicit user acknowledgement before prompting.","code_snippet":"      const errText = stderr.trim().toLowerCase();\n      if (errText.includes('user canceled') || errText.includes('denied') || errText.includes('interaction not allowed')) {\n        throw new CookieImportError(\n          `Keychain access denied. Click \"Allow\" in the macOS dialog for \"${service}\".`,\n          'keychain_denied',\n          'retry',\n        );","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"044e59b8cb232d8d2a59d6f4b1e8fe2b50ce1a35abe47e0398df30fd491b561c","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":315,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-9c8cd18f431e47b3946cb1ac075a7ef0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file claims the routes are 'localhost-only' and unauthenticated, but this handler does not verify the request origin, host, or client address before performing sensitive cookie listing, decryption, import, and removal operations. If the surrounding server is exposed beyond localhost or proxied unexpectedly, an attacker could invoke these endpoints to access local browser cookie material and manipulate the automation session.","remediation":"Enforce local-only access in code by validating the listening interface and rejecting any request whose client address or Host is not loopback. Add authentication/authorization such as a per-session secret token, and require CSRF-resistant request validation for state-changing endpoints.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-7316341429bb4847a9747983cdc66893","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":270,"end_line":306},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `cookie-import-browser` command reaches outside the skill's stated QA/browser-automation scope and imports cookies from installed local browsers, which are highly sensitive authentication artifacts. This can grant access to unrelated user sessions and effectively exfiltrate or reuse local credentials inside the automation context, making compromise of third-party accounts or environments possible.","remediation":"Remove browser-cookie extraction entirely from this skill, or gate it behind a separate explicitly consented tool with strong user-visible warnings and least-privilege scoping. If retention is necessary, require explicit confirmation per import, restrict allowed domains to a user-approved allowlist, avoid importing non-target cookies, and add auditing for every import attempt.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":270,"end_line":306}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-bd3cb71d915745a0b21e53114a60b21a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1046,"end_line":1055},"finding":null,"explanation":"Arbitrary request header injection is a powerful primitive that enables spoofing authentication, API keys, origin-related metadata, and other trust signals on outbound requests. In a tool that can browse arbitrary URLs, this can be abused for credential misuse, SSRF-like testing against internal apps, or unauthorized access under forged headers.","remediation":"Disallow arbitrary header injection by default and permit only a minimal allowlist needed for QA. Explicitly block sensitive headers such as `Authorization`, `Cookie`, and proxy/internal routing headers unless an elevated, user-approved mode is enabled, and scope custom headers to approved domains.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1046,"end_line":1055}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-1ea48604c68c42a7a8d76a1bfbcd0575","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1439,"end_line":1458},"finding":null,"explanation":"Cookie import from local files enables the browser to assume arbitrary session state, including impersonating existing authenticated users if session cookies are supplied. Combined with arbitrary navigation and page scripting, this creates a direct pathway to account/session takeover within the automated browser.","remediation":"Remove cookie import for general use or require explicit privileged mode with prominent warnings and consent. Validate cookie provenance, restrict imports to approved domains/environments, prevent importing high-risk session cookies by default, and log/audit all cookie import activity.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1439,"end_line":1458}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-38b2baa56a1647bdaaa0bec0bea6a2c2","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1665,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"\n  test('eval rejects path traversal with ..', async () => {\n    try {\n      await handleReadCommand('eval', ['../../etc/passwd'], bm);\n      expect(true).toBe(false);\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      expect(err.message).toContain('Path traversal');","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ac75eea6ed115d0252fb13bbb10e9c4421764d5a7612787edcde6a78569d8f88","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1665,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-38b2baa56a1647bdaaa0bec0bea6a2c2","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1674,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"\n  test('eval rejects path traversal with ..', async () => {\n    try {\n      await handleReadCommand('eval', ['../../etc/passwd'], bm);\n      exp