ions and safety constraints. This can degrade agent performance or bypass safety boundaries.","remediation":"Implement context-window management that detects and rejects padding or stuffing attempts. Prioritize system instructions over user-injected content.","code_snippet":"  'perf':    { category: 'Inspection', description: 'Page load timings' },\n  // Interaction\n  'click':   { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Click element', usage: 'click <sel>' },\n  'fill':    { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Fill input', usage: 'fill <sel> <val>' },\n  'select':  { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Select dropdown option by value, label, or visible text', usage: 'select <sel> <val>' },\n  'hover':   { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Hover element', usage: 'hover <sel>' },\n  'type':    { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Type into focused element', usage: 'type <text>' },","intent":null,"tags":["Memory Poisoning","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7a90427092f85fe236c42657231437965bc09b95a5fbaa72aace3ea4e8ef61d7","occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/commands.ts","start_line":64,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"MP2","finding_id":"finding-d1f9ee0ff308453c8fd1fa3108b0b9f1","category":"Memory Poisoning","pattern":"Context Window Stuffing","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":155,"end_line":null},"finding":"Fill input","explanation":"Skill attempts to fill the context window with filler content, displacing legitimate instructions and safety constraints. This can degrade agent performance or bypass safety boundaries.","remediation":"Implement context-window management that detects and rejects padding or stuffing attempts. Prioritize system instructions over user-injected content.","code_snippet":"  'perf':    { category: 'Inspection', description: 'Page load timings' },\n  // Interaction\n  'click':   { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Click element', usage: 'click <sel>' },\n  'fill':    { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Fill input', usage: 'fill <sel> <val>' },\n  'select':  { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Select dropdown option by value, label, or visible text', usage: 'select <sel> <val>' },\n  'hover':   { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Hover element', usage: 'hover <sel>' },\n  'type':    { category: 'Interaction', description: 'Type into focused element', usage: 'type <text>' },","intent":null,"tags":["Memory Poisoning","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7a90427092f85fe236c42657231437965bc09b95a5fbaa72aace3ea4e8ef61d7","occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":155,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-6266047b8ebd4db1adfadc7cb1396827","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":28,"end_line":36},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill manifest frames this as a fast headless browser for QA testing websites, but this file spawns git commands to discover the repository root and remote origin metadata. Repository interrogation is not an obvious requirement for browser automation itself and introduces local-environment access beyond the stated testing scope.","remediation":"Remove git-dependent behavior unless it is essential, or document this capability explicitly in the manifest as part of how the skill manages project-local state and naming.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":28,"end_line":36}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-eaa3fd8ea4774eb6930f4d6a65d22773","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":93,"end_line":100},"finding":null,"explanation":"ensureStateDir() silently edits the parent project's .gitignore as a side effect of creating runtime state. Modifying repository files is outside the minimal need for browser automation and can unexpectedly alter source-control behavior, especially because projectDir can be derived from an environment-controlled BROWSE_STATE_FILE path.","remediation":"Do not auto-modify .gitignore during normal initialization. Instead, print a one-time notice instructing the user to add .gstack/ manually, or gate the change behind an explicit opt-in flag/interactive confirmation. Also validate that projectDir is the intended workspace before writing any repository file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":93,"end_line":100}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ae89ef4cbf5e4ac3aa3e3a22cd2e991f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":93,"end_line":100},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code appends to .gitignore without any user-facing warning, confirmation, or opt-in, creating an undocumented persistent change to the repository. In an agent skill context, silent mutation of tracked project configuration is more dangerous because users may invoke the skill expecting ephemeral browser testing, not source-control side effects.","remediation":"Require explicit consent before editing .gitignore, such as a --update-gitignore flag or interactive prompt. Prefer surfacing a warning with the exact line to add manually, and log the decision clearly so repository changes are intentional and auditable.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/config.ts","start_line":93,"end_line":100}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9dcbb81dc4d140cd8514226317b79973","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":139,"end_line":148},"finding":null,"explanation":"`importCookies` performs sensitive cookie import/decryption with no built-in user-facing disclosure, confirmation, or visibility at the API entry point. That increases the risk of silent credential harvesting or accidental import of real personal sessions during routine QA usage.","remediation":"Add an explicit consent and warning step at the import entry point that states the function will access local browser cookies and macOS Keychain data. Require affirmative opt-in for each import, log the target browser/profile/domains, and block operation unless the caller marks the request as an acknowledged sensitive action.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-import-browser.ts","start_line":139,"end_line":148}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-b6b434aab39848e09ca338248fdca6d5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a headless browser skill for navigating pages, interacting with elements, verifying UI state, screenshots, and form testing. This file adds a localhost HTTP API for enumerating installed browsers, reading browser cookie domains, decrypting stored cookies, and injecting them into the Playwright session, which is materially broader than the stated testing/dogfooding behavior.","remediation":"Update the manifest to explicitly disclose browser-cookie import/decryption capabilities and their purpose, or remove/disable these routes if cookie extraction is outside the intended skill scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-9133758681dc42bd91145ce5fd40cf51","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":106,"end_line":137},"finding":null,"explanation":"Decrypting cookies from other installed browsers and importing them into the active Playwright context is a sensitive capability. While browser automation is in scope, credential/session extraction from local browser stores is not an obvious or necessary requirement of the manifest’s described QA and dogfooding use cases.","remediation":"Constrain the feature behind explicit opt-in, document it clearly in the skill description, and limit it to narrowly justified scenarios such as user-authorized session portability for testing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":106,"end_line":137}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e453b49514eb4b879cf5dd1b3c5b1c65","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":121,"end_line":137},"finding":null,"explanation":"This route decrypts browser cookies and imports them into a Playwright session, which is a privacy-sensitive operation involving user data. Although there is a console log after completion, there is no pre-action confirmation, warning comment/docstring about the sensitivity of the import endpoint itself, or other user-facing disclosure in this file.","remediation":"Add a user-facing warning or confirmation before importing cookies, and document clearly in code comments or associated skill documentation that this endpoint decrypts browser cookies and injects them into the automation session.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":121,"end_line":137}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e4d154f800a2418f8fcd9d0f872cbe47","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":154,"end_line":176},"finding":null,"explanation":"The remove route performs a destructive state-changing action by clearing cookies for specified domains from the Playwright context. This file logs the removal after it happens, but it does not present a prior warning, confirmation, or explanatory disclosure for the destructive operation.","remediation":"Add an explicit confirmation or user-visible warning before clearing cookies, and document in code comments or skill documentation that the route removes cookies from the current browser context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-routes.ts","start_line":154,"end_line":176}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-7e2c403f910e4b93b68fb6b3aad5c7fc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-ui.ts","start_line":260,"end_line":284},"finding":null,"explanation":"The UI allows importing cookies from local browsers into the active session and removing them again without any explicit warning, confirmation, or explanation of the security consequences. In this skill context, cookie import can silently authenticate the headless browser as another user/account and materially change test behavior, increasing the risk of unintended session takeover, cross-account actions, or confusing operator mistakes.","remediation":"Add a clear, persistent warning near the import/remove controls explaining that imported cookies modify the current session and may authenticate the browser as another account. Require explicit confirmation before import, show which browser/domains will be affected, and provide an easy way to review and clear imported cookies; ideally also scope imports narrowly and log/audit these actions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/cookie-picker-ui.ts","start_line":260,"end_line":284}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-66dbce557624465d84c4f31d9f3a7617","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":2,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file header describes these commands as extracting data \"without side effects,\" which implies read-only behavior. However, the `storage` command supports `set` to write to `localStorage`, and the `console`, `network`, and `dialog` commands support `--clear`, which mutates captured state rather than merely reading it.","remediation":"Update the module documentation to accurately describe that most commands are read-oriented but some subcommands mutate browser storage or internal buffers, or split mutating behaviors into separate write commands.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":2,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-82c0212c955b447ab3b1db314fab5c2d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":264,"end_line":266},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `cookies` command returns all browser context cookies, which may include session identifiers, CSRF tokens, or other sensitive authentication material. In an agent skill that can navigate arbitrary sites, exposing this data without any warning, scoping, or redaction can leak credentials to logs, users, or higher-level orchestration layers.","remediation":"Redact or omit sensitive cookie fields by default, and require an explicit privileged mode to access full cookie data. Add user-facing disclosure, origin scoping, and audit logging, and consider returning only metadata unless full values are strictly necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":264,"end_line":266}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-685d788ea9224c0ea588d720770d09a7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":269,"end_line":275},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `storage set` path allows mutation of page localStorage inside a module explicitly framed as read-only, which can alter application state, feature flags, auth flows, or test outcomes unexpectedly. In a headless browser automation skill, this increases the risk of confusing operators or downstream agents into performing state-changing actions under a supposedly safe/read-only interface.","remediation":"Remove `storage set` from the read command handler and place it in a separate write/mutate command group with explicit naming and confirmation semantics. If storage mutation is required, gate it behind an opt-in flag, audit logging, and clear user-facing warnings that the action changes page state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":269,"end_line":275}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6418fcd699f74a9d93836071600f95c6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":269,"end_line":280},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `storage` command exposes all `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` contents and also supports writing values, which may reveal tokens, PII, app secrets, or alter client-side security state. Because this skill is designed for broad browser inspection across arbitrary URLs, unrestricted storage access is more dangerous than in a narrowly scoped testing-only tool and can enable both data exfiltration and state manipulation.","remediation":"Split inspection and mutation into separate commands and require explicit authorization for each. Redact sensitive values by default, scope access to approved origins, warn users before returning storage contents, and log all reads/writes of browser storage for auditability.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/read-commands.ts","start_line":269,"end_line":280}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-d8daf6c5b4f94b35bbbbbcd9dc0be6c1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"browse/src/snapshot.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file-level documentation explicitly describes the snapshot architecture as 'no DOM mutation'. However, when `--annotate` is used, the implementation calls `page.evaluate` to create `<div>` and `<span>` overlay nodes and appends them to `document.body`, temporarily modifying the DOM before cleanup. This is an active contradiction between the documented intent and actual behavior.","remediation":"Update the header documentation to disclose that annotation mode temporarily injects overlay elements into the page DOM, or redesign annotation to avoid in-page DOM mutation if the 'no DOM mutation' guarantee is intended to be strict.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/snapshot.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-943e162b875d410f9ea97b71a51e2ac0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":239,"end_line":251},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code claims to prevent arbitrary file reads, but it only restricts absolute paths while still allowing caller-controlled relative paths anywhere under the working tree. That enables reading arbitrary JSON files from the repository or execution directory and treating them as cookie material, which can expose secrets or internal data if an attacker can influence the path.","remediation":"Enforce a dedicated safe import directory for cookie files and resolve all paths against that directory before access. Reject any path outside the allowlisted directory, regardless of whether it is absolute or relative, and consider requiring a fixed filename pattern or explicit file selection API instead of raw path input.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":239,"end_line":251}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ffcebdaeb6c94254b5f02006811f4ca2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":270,"end_line":287},"finding":null,"explanation":"Importing cookies from installed browsers accesses sensitive session tokens, but this file provides no explicit warning, confirmation step, or consent barrier before the action occurs in direct import mode. In the context of an automation skill, this increases the risk that powerful authentication artifacts are imported and then used or exposed without the user understanding the security implications.","remediation":"Add explicit user-facing warnings and an affirmative consent step before any browser-cookie import. Clearly disclose what data will be accessed, for which domains, from which browser, and provide a chance to cancel; also log the action and minimize imported cookies to only those strictly required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":270,"end_line":287}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-f290c265820648fb8f8c14fe3316f35f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":290,"end_line":301},"finding":null,"explanation":"Spawning the OS `open` command to launch a local picker UI introduces an unnecessary side effect for a supposedly headless QA tool and expands the trust boundary from browser automation into host-level process execution. While the URL is locally constructed, the behavior can surprise users, trigger local applications, and facilitate misuse of the cookie-import flow by nudging the operator into approving sensitive cookie access.","remediation":"Avoid spawning host OS commands from this skill. Return the local picker URL to the caller and require the user to open it manually, or move the picker into an already-existing authenticated UI with explicit warnings and consent before any cookie access occurs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/write-commands.ts","start_line":290,"end_line":301}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-25521b6e88e04e3bb5adc8d98623d44b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":135,"end_line":183},"finding":null,"explanation":"The tests confirm the skill exposes arbitrary JavaScript execution via `js` and file-backed `eval`, allowing callers to run unrestricted code inside any loaded page context. In a browser automation skill that can navigate arbitrary URLs, this meaningfully expands capability beyond ordinary QA interactions and can be abused to extract DOM data, tokens, local/session storage, or perform actions in authenticated sessions.","remediation":"Either remove `js`/`eval` entirely or gate them behind an explicit high-trust mode with strong user consent and documentation. If retained, restrict execution to an allowlisted set of read-only helpers, disable file-backed eval, audit/limit accessible browser APIs, and update the manifest to accurately disclose this high-risk capability.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":135,"end_line":183}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-2cecbaaf3cdf4ff2bd49711508cef283","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1014,"end_line":1055},"finding":null,"explanation":"These tests show support for cookie setting/import and arbitrary header manipulation, capabilities not reflected in the manifest description. Those features allow request/session tampering and can be used to impersonate users, bypass intended browser state, or send sensitive/custom auth material to arbitrary destinations.","remediation":"Document these capabilities explicitly and require elevated permission for stateful/session-modifying features. Narrow them to well-justified QA use cases, add destination scoping/allowlists, block sensitive header names unless explicitly approved, and require explicit confirmation before importing cookies or mutating authenticated session state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/commands.test.ts","start_line":1014,"end_line":1055}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f9fbd763459c49308ccdefffbdffb934","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"browse/test/fixtures/qa-eval-checkout.html","start_line":97,"end_line":104},"finding":null,"explanation":"This HTML/JS code collects email, address, and credit-card data and attempts to submit card details to a payment API via `stripe.createPaymentMethod`, but there is no visible notice, comment, or disclosure to the user about payment processing or transmission of sensitive data. Under the code-file criteria, sensitive data handling and network-bound payment operations should have some form of user-facing warning or explanatory disclosure.","remediation":"Add a visible notice near the payment section or submit button explaining that payment details will be processed by Stripe and that personal/shipping information is collected for order fulfillment. Also consider adding a brief comment or documentation note describing the payment-processing behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/fixtures/qa-eval-checkout.html","start_line":97,"end_line":104}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-20ae45481b1645b29382e5724b8622b2","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write\n  - Edit\n  - Grep\n  - Glob\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED from SKILL.md.tmpl — do not edit directly -->\n<!-- Regenerate: bun run gen:skill-docs -->\n\n## Preamble (run first)\n\n```bash","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"allowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - Write\n  - Edit\n  - Grep\n  - Glob","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"46ea3340f04bd7df0213c32ead584e3339086bc92bbdcd8670b5b5afdb6cd909","occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-5527a77d3587446a897ff36b8219c313","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":34},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises a documentation-update workflow, but its preamble also triggers gstack self-update logic and reads auxiliary skill files outside the target repository. That expands scope beyond user-expected doc edits and introduces unrelated side effects before the main task begins, violating least surprise and least privilege.","remediation":"Remove self-update behavior from this skill entirely, or move it to an explicit opt-in maintenance step with clear disclosure. Limit startup actions to repository-local checks required for documentation work, and do not read or execute other skill files from the user's home directory automatically.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":34}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-4259b5029a6e4709b603496fae2412f1","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack","explanation":"The preamble creates and maintains session-tracking files under ~/.gstack/sessions, establishing persistent state outside the repository without clear user consent. Hidden session persistence can be abused for tracking, cross-task state leakage, or simply violating user expectations about the skill's scope.","remediation":"Eliminate persistent session markers from this skill, or document them clearly and obtain explicit opt-in. If session tracking is required by the platform, handle it in trusted infrastructure rather than inside task-specific skill instructions.","code_snippet":"```bash\n_UPD=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || .claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || true)\n[ -n \"$_UPD\" ] && echo \"$_UPD\" || true\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin -120 -type f 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nfind ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin +120 -type f -delete 2>/dev/null || true","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5e808e4c235a730213d17543b3ecd63b866e66e9ee00e0707fa038544ff15826","occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-009d4d1bc2794dd1b619d693176c2b94","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28},"finding":null,"explanation":"The preamble deletes files in ~/.gstack/sessions older than 120 minutes without notifying the user. Even if intended as cleanup, silent deletion outside the repository is a destructive side effect unrelated to documentation editing and could remove state the user expected to persist.","remediation":"Do not delete files in the preamble. If cleanup is necessary, confine it to an application-owned cache with documented retention policy and explicit user disclosure, or perform it only after opt-in confirmation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-fd314952c07746c1a3dc0705f774748e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":34,"end_line":null},"finding":"write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n\n**ALWAYS follow this structure for every Ask","explanation":"The instruction to write snooze state for upgrades if declined introduces additional persistent state in the user's home directory, unrelated to documentation release work. This broadens the skill into preference management and creates hidden cross-session behavior without adequate disclosure.","remediation":"Do not manage upgrade snooze state from this skill. Move update preference persistence into a dedicated updater flow with explicit consent and documented storage behavior.","code_snippet":"echo \"BRANCH: $_BRANCH\"\n```\n\nIf output shows `UPGRADE_AVAILABLE <old> <new>`: read `~/.claude/skills/gstack/gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md` and follow the \"Inline upgrade flow\" (auto-upgrade if configured, otherwise AskUserQuestion with 4 options, write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"897ec9f9d58b2e14e9f5e1b059f4c1cef2b28ccbca8277d62d296f27bf766e10","occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":34,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-2a6a0bccf7514c599a5e617c14ecdbcc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"Contributor mode authorizes creation of feedback files under the user's home directory about gstack itself, which is unrelated to updating project documentation. This adds hidden write behavior and persistent side effects outside the repo, increasing the attack surface and violating the principle of task-bounded permissions.","remediation":"Remove contributor-report writing from this skill, or gate it behind separate explicit user consent. Constrain all writes to the repository workspace unless the user has directly invoked a feedback-reporting workflow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ede1dd8980884c37982c572f923c705d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":58,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"The contributor-mode instructions direct the agent to write field reports into ~/.gstack/contributor-logs without an upfront warning in the skill description. This creates persistent files outside the project and can surprise users who believed the workflow was limited to repository documentation changes.","remediation":"Add clear disclosure in the skill description and require explicit consent before any home-directory writes. Prefer storing such reports inside the repository or in a dedicated, separately invoked reporting skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":58,"end_line":58}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-711540c5a4714155b1b4d585bf33bdf8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":89,"end_line":100},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest says the skill reads project docs, cross-references diffs, updates documentation files, cleans TODOS, and optionally bumps VERSION. The code also queries PR metadata with gh and later edits the PR body, introducing external GitHub API interactions that are not disclosed in the description. While related to release workflow convenience, this is not necessary to the core document-update purpose as stated.","remediation":"Either narrow the implementation to repository-local documentation updates only, or update the manifest to explicitly state that the skill may inspect PR metadata and update the PR description on GitHub.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":89,"end_line":100}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-f4c23204318744d5a3aae89b55c5a39c","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":130,"end_line":null},"finding":"without asking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n**NEVER do:**\n- Overwrite, replace, or regenerate CHANGELOG entries — polish wording only, preserve all content\n- Bump VERSION without asking — always use AskUserQuestion for version changes\n- Use `Write` tool on CHANGELOG.md — always use `Edit` with exact `old_string` matches\n\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8dc77d3dce9ba1f2672e813265a1b1a0c8594866ef38a4e978bf4f4451795465","occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":130,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-d21ef910ced5400eb69a470e12489a90","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":310,"end_line":null},"finding":"WITHOUT ASKING","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n## Step 8: VERSION Bump Question\n\n**CRITICAL — NEVER BUMP VERSION WITHOUT ASKING.**\n\n1. **If VERSION does not exist:** Skip silently.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8eca02cd90fa0e6d92d3f7868829adf6b8570749a9fb77090b092fd298d03e7f","occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":310,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3c922e7a6a6d4642941b999d735338f3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":367,"end_line":370},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow pushes commits to the current branch automatically, but this remote side effect is not prominently disclosed in the skill description. Users may authorize a doc-update skill expecting local edits only, not immediate publication to the remote repository.","remediation":"Disclose push behavior prominently in metadata and pause for explicit confirmation before running git push. A safer design is to create the commit locally and let the user decide whether to push.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"document-release/SKILL.md","start_line":367,"end_line":370}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-7f6d63bbb6d5454b90a633569cf37398","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED from SKILL.md.tmpl — do not edit directly -->\n<!-- Regenerate: bun run gen:skill-docs -->\n\n# /gstack-upgrade\n\nUpgrade gstack to the latest version and","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"allowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - Write\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED from SKILL.md.tmpl — do not edit directly -->","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"891e6053a419cd657ab4fa55185be552ef3a2a46bfb4be638f2d0179bd2d67ec","occurrences":[{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-743a91e84a3d49d5a561df8d2495600d","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write snooze state with escalating backoff (first snooze = 24h, second = 48h, third+ = 1 week), then continue with the current skill. Do not mention the upgrade again.\n```bash\n_SNOOZE_FILE=~/.gstack/u","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"```\nTell user: \"Auto-upgrade enabled. Future updates will install automatically.\" Then proceed to Step 2.\n\n**If \"Not now\":** Write snooze state with escalating backoff (first snooze = 24h, second = 48h, third+ = 1 week), then continue with the current skill. Do not mention the upgrade again.\n```bash\n_SNOOZE_FILE=~/.gstack/update-snoozed\n_REMOTE_VER=\"{new}\"","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0664443dbd7fe84f752fde02203348b9342025bacd453af128ed88574a3a1949","occurrences":[{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1dc673e8dd3f4eefb3998797a4aacacd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":121,"end_line":129},"finding":null,"explanation":"The vendored upgrade flow replaces the existing install by moving it aside, swapping in a freshly cloned directory, running setup, and then deleting backups. If setup fails or the clone is incomplete, the skill can leave the installation broken or delete the only recoverable copy, and the description does not prominently warn users about these destructive actions beforehand.","remediation":"Add an explicit pre-execution warning and confirmation for any operation that replaces or deletes directories. Make the vendored upgrade transactional: verify clone integrity first, run setup successfully before deleting backups, and automatically restore from .bak on any failure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":121,"end_line":129}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-217e16599d844cb989f2f3a8ffa2c7e6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":149,"end_line":157},"finding":null,"explanation":"The local vendored sync path overwrites another gstack directory, strips its .git metadata, runs setup, and then deletes the backup. This can destroy local modifications or repository history in a secondary copy without a clear, upfront warning or a safe rollback path if copy/setup fails.","remediation":"Require separate confirmation before modifying a second directory and clearly state that local changes and VCS metadata may be lost. Preserve .git unless the user opts in, validate the target path, and keep the backup until the copied install and setup complete successfully.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":149,"end_line":157}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-51831d8569be4684a447d31de771ab3d","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":159,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write marker + clear cache\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack\necho \"$OLD_VERSION\" > ~/.gstack/just-upgraded-from\nrm -f ~/.gstack/last-update-check\nrm -f ~/.gstack/update-snoozed\n```\n\n### Step 6: Show What's ","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"```\nTell user: \"Also updated vendored copy at `$LOCAL_GSTACK` — commit `.claude/skills/gstack/` when you're ready.\"\n\n### Step 5: Write marker + clear cache\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e551bd9099921c136c173f8ad9dcc6041bfd1a28381acece72503a05e5370ada","occurrences":[{"file":"gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md","start_line":159,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-227f9d532fd3456fb5477eb8b1f5e9ea","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description explains the skill's review style and modes, but it does not state when the skill should be invoked versus when similar planning or review requests should not use it. For a markdown skill file, this broad description can overlap with many ordinary requests for plan feedback or review, increasing the chance of unintended invocation.","remediation":"Add explicit trigger guidance such as concrete invocation phrases, required context (for example, only when reviewing a written implementation plan), and negative examples showing nearby requests that should not activate this skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-6dae2bf580fd4b75895406ee62b68d01","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":33},"finding":null,"explanation":"This plan-review skill embeds gstack browser-tooling update and upgrade-flow instructions that are unrelated to its stated purpose. That mismatch increases the chance an agent will invoke external tooling and follow side-effecting workflows under false pretenses, weakening user trust and expanding the operational attack surface.","remediation":"Remove browser-specific preamble and upgrade-flow content from this skill, or factor shared bootstrap logic into a narrowly scoped, opt-in common include. Ensure the skill only references tools and workflows necessary for read-only plan review, and document any external tool dependency explicitly in the skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":33}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-723c9c21b0ea4caeb0cdd1b046eb26f9","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack","explanation":"Creating and maintaining ~/.gstack/sessions entries establishes persistent session tracking on the local machine. Even lightweight persistence can accumulate behavioral metadata over time and is especially risky when embedded in a skill that presents itself as a review-only workflow.","remediation":"Remove session-file creation and retention from the skill, or replace it with in-memory/session-scoped tracking that does not touch disk. If persistence is required, disclose retention behavior, minimize stored data, and require explicit consent.","code_snippet":"```bash\n_UPD=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || .claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || true)\n[ -n \"$_UPD\" ] && echo \"$_UPD\" || true\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin -120 -type f 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nfind ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin +120 -type f -delete 2>/dev/null || true","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5e808e4c235a730213d17543b3ecd63b866e66e9ee00e0707fa038544ff15826","occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-a8c9f974d5b343d29ace4d5af9cb37a3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":27},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill says not to make code changes, but its preamble still creates session files and deletes old ones in ~/.gstack/sessions. Even if it avoids modifying repository code, it still performs filesystem mutations, which is a dangerous inconsistency because it can mislead users and bypass expectations of a non-mutating review flow.","remediation":"Align the documentation and behavior: either make the skill fully non-mutating or clearly disclose and justify every filesystem write. Prefer eliminating the session-touch and cleanup behavior entirely from this skill; if session tracking is necessary, move it to a trusted wrapper outside the skill content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":27}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-ff6194963f964644944da271a9cdde41","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n\n**ALWAYS follow this structure for every Ask","explanation":"The upgrade-flow instructions mention writing snooze state if the user declines an upgrade, which introduces additional persistent local state unrelated to the plan-review task. This compounds the hidden-persistence problem by allowing the skill to alter long-lived configuration or preference state without being central to the user’s requested work.","remediation":"Remove upgrade-state persistence from this skill entirely and handle upgrades in a separate, clearly labeled maintenance skill or wrapper. Any preference or snooze-state writes should be explicit, user-approved, and documented up front.","code_snippet":"echo \"BRANCH: $_BRANCH\"\n```\n\nIf output shows `UPGRADE_AVAILABLE <old> <new>`: read `~/.claude/skills/gstack/gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md` and follow the \"Inline upgrade flow\" (auto-upgrade if configured, otherwise AskUserQuestion with 4 options, write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"897ec9f9d58b2e14e9f5e1b059f4c1cef2b28ccbca8277d62d296f27bf766e10","occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5a82522514c1461b999e02eb09842938","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":47,"end_line":82},"finding":null,"explanation":"The contributor-mode instructions direct the agent to generate and write telemetry-style field reports to ~/.gstack/contributor-logs during normal use. That creates undisclosed local writes unrelated to the user’s review task and can leak task context, errors, or repository details into persistent files without clear consent.","remediation":"Remove automatic contributor logging from this skill, or gate it behind explicit user opt-in with clear disclosure of what will be written and where. If feedback collection is required, use a separate maintenance workflow or transient, non-persistent reporting path.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":47,"end_line":82}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b9521e24703e41a9ae15f2b2fac3c173","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":57,"end_line":82},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to write contributor reports to the user’s filesystem without prominent user-facing disclosure in the skill description. Hidden or under-disclosed persistence is risky because users may not realize their prompts, outputs, or environment details are being stored locally.","remediation":"Add explicit disclosure in the skill metadata that local files may be written, including paths and purpose, and require user consent before any write. Better yet, remove filesystem-report writing from this skill and keep plan review strictly non-persistent.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":57,"end_line":82}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-371eb077428b4e149795a7ff9a619931","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"plan-eng-review/SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write\n  - Grep\n  - 