 but its preamble performs unrelated gstack self-maintenance tasks such as upgrade checks and session bookkeeping in the user's home directory. This violates least surprise and expands the skill's behavior beyond its stated purpose, creating hidden side effects and additional attack surface before the core task even begins.","remediation":"Remove upgrade checks, session tracking, and other gstack-maintenance actions from this skill. Keep the preamble limited to repo-local setup needed for retrospective generation, and explicitly disclose any non-repo side effects in the skill description if they are truly necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":32}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-67dcdb060f12409bab0e70d8ca8d9c2a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":32},"finding":null,"explanation":"Reading global gstack upgrade state and conditionally executing an upgrade flow is not necessary to analyze a git repository's history. Tying retrospective execution to global tool-update state introduces unrelated control flow and may cause the agent to read additional instructions or write snooze state outside the repo.","remediation":"Remove the upgrade-state logic from this skill entirely. Handle tool updates in a dedicated bootstrap or package-management workflow rather than inside unrelated business skills.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":32}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-ef0a40d753b14940bc5a9c9b2c05bd81","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\