not manage upgrade snooze state from this skill. Move update prompting and snooze persistence into a separate, explicitly authorized update workflow.","code_snippet":"echo \"BRANCH: $_BRANCH\"\n```\n\nIf output shows `UPGRADE_AVAILABLE <old> <new>`: read `~/.claude/skills/gstack/gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md` and follow the \"Inline upgrade flow\" (auto-upgrade if configured, otherwise AskUserQuestion with 4 options, write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"897ec9f9d58b2e14e9f5e1b059f4c1cef2b28ccbca8277d62d296f27bf766e10","occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e1ae65ed993e4e9aba08741f219d771f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":96},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill analyzes per-person contributions and local history artifacts without an explicit privacy notice, even though it profiles named individuals' work patterns and may read local auxiliary files. That creates a meaningful transparency issue because users may not realize the breadth of personal/team activity being summarized and persisted.","remediation":"Add a clear privacy disclosure to the skill description and runtime output describing what data is read, how per-person metrics are computed, and what gets stored. Provide an option to anonymize contributors or disable persistence.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":96}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-3322b2b37674443d8a1e2c7a954dbba4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":97},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill aggregates and outputs per-person contribution patterns, coding hours, session timing, and related behavioral data derived from repo history and local metadata. Persisting and displaying this kind of employee/activity profiling can expose sensitive work-pattern information beyond what is necessary for a simple retrospective.","remediation":"Minimize personal-data collection and default to aggregate team-level reporting. Add opt-in controls for named contributor analysis, redact or anonymize time-pattern data where possible, and document retention of any derived analytics.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":97}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-2793f666ed26404885b8e3c57e6096f7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":162,"end_line":166},"finding":null,"explanation":"Reading local history files such as greptile-history and then incorporating derived conclusions into reports and saved snapshots broadens disclosure beyond current repository state. This can unintentionally surface prior tool outputs or local-only context that users did not expect to be included in a sharable retro artifact.","remediation":"Limit inputs to repository data unless the user explicitly opts into enriching the retro with external local history. Clearly label each external source used and avoid persisting derived data from local-only files by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":162,"end_line":166}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-84c60b45f7cb473fb5c2150219272ba3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":354,"end_line":371},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill persists retrospective snapshots into .context/retros within the repository, but the top-level description does not clearly warn that invoking the skill will create repo files. In environments with strict cleanliness, CI triggers, or sensitive contribution analytics, unexpected writes can create privacy, workflow, and change-management issues.","remediation":"Disclose snapshot persistence prominently in the skill description and first-run behavior. Prefer asking for consent before the initial write, and offer a no-persist mode or alternate output location outside the repo.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":354,"end_line":371}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-59b781f198ec49a2a5edeac96f7ddb66","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write tool to save the JSON file with this schema:\n```json\n{\n  \"date\": \"2026-03-08\",\n  \"window\": \"7d\",\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"commits\": 47,\n    \"contributors\": 3,\n    \"prs_merged\": 12,\n    \"insertions\": ","explanation":"Persisting retro snapshots is intentional functionality here, so it is not inherently malicious, but it does create durable state that can expose team analytics and alter the repo. Because the write is repo-local and documented later in the skill, the issue is more about transparency and privacy than pure persistence alone.","remediation":"Keep persistence optional and clearly disclosed up front. Ask before the first write, support a dry-run/no-save mode, and consider storing snapshots in a non-versioned path unless the user explicitly wants them tracked.","code_snippet":"# Save as .context/retros/${today}-${next}.json\n```\n\nUse the Write tool to save the JSON file with this schema:\n```json\n{\n  \"date\": \"2026-03-08\",","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7ae634874e6540783133086c23e1a5af71835047a41653a8cc6e464deaa41dc2","occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-963c75e9971d4d51a55b57a3abbd8566","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":401},"finding":null,"explanation":"The snapshot schema stores named author statistics and a tweetable summary, creating durable records of contributor behavior and project activity that may later be committed, shared, or reused out of context. This increases privacy and disclosure risk, especially in team settings where work-pattern analytics can be sensitive.","remediation":"Reduce persistence to the minimum necessary: omit named author stats by default, avoid generating tweetable summaries unless explicitly requested, and provide anonymization/redaction options. Store snapshots outside version-controlled paths unless the user intentionally chooses repo persistence.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":371,"end_line":401}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-7e65af7f78b941ffb547bfe0cf0e96b5","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write\n  - Grep\n  - Glob\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED from SKILL.md.tmpl — do not edit directly -->\n<!-- Regenerate: bun run gen:skill-docs -->\n\n## Preamble (run first)\n\n```bash\n_UPD=$(~","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - Edit\n  - Write\n  - Grep\n  - Glob\n  - AskUserQuestion","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3d78b0d8c469b6b3434a78c81804f468a3f122261ce4ab8ee5d511c86b700ed2","occurrences":[{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-b07f26ad479a402295c2a5259cc4e575","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":33},"finding":null,"explanation":"A PR review skill should be narrowly scoped to analyzing repository changes, but this section injects unrelated gstack update handling and browser-tooling lifecycle behavior. That expands the skill's authority and execution path beyond the user's requested task, creating unnecessary side effects and an avoidable trust boundary with external/local tool management logic.","remediation":"Remove the update-check and upgrade-handling behavior from this skill's preamble. Keep the review workflow limited to branch detection and read-only repo analysis, and move any tool self-management into a separate explicitly-invoked maintenance skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":33}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-c3fe14a1320a4f5286364dfb7b427080","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack","explanation":"Creating and pruning files under ~/.gstack/sessions establishes persistent session tracking for a PR review workflow that should primarily inspect repository state. This is a side effect outside the user's task and can be used to record agent activity over time, expanding privacy and statefulness risks unnecessarily.","remediation":"Remove session file creation/deletion from the review preamble. If session accounting is operationally necessary, move it to the platform runtime rather than embedding it in user-facing skills, and disclose/obtain consent for any persistence.","code_snippet":"```bash\n_UPD=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || .claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || true)\n[ -n \"$_UPD\" ] && echo \"$_UPD\" || true\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin -120 -type f 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nfind ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin +120 -type f -delete 2>/dev/null || true","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5e808e4c235a730213d17543b3ecd63b866e66e9ee00e0707fa038544ff15826","occurrences":[{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-f488f0d4fc754605b01df41b0da63cb4","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n\n**ALWAYS follow this structure for every Ask","explanation":"Writing upgrade snooze state introduces durable local state changes unrelated to code review and ties a repository-analysis workflow to tool-maintenance preferences. This persistence is unnecessary for the task and increases the chance of hidden behavior, user surprise, and policy bypass through cross-run state.","remediation":"Eliminate snooze-state writes from this skill. Keep review workflows stateless except for artifacts explicitly requested by the user, and isolate upgrade preferences to a separate dedicated settings or maintenance path.","code_snip