o write structured logs to disk without being part of the user's requested objective. This unnecessary persistence increases privacy and integrity risk by creating side-channel records of user activity and tool behavior.","remediation":"Remove automatic contributor report generation from this skill. If tool feedback is desired, place it in a separate opt-in command and minimize stored content, retention, and default write behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"review/SKILL.md","start_line":51,"end_line":82}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-aea242c91d0245bdadf772b0d9c7847b","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"review/checklist.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null},"finding":"without checking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n#### Test Gaps\n- Negative-path tests that assert type/status but not the side effects (URL attached? field populated? callback fired?)\n- Assertions on string content without checking format (e.g., asserting title present but not URL format)\n- `.expects(:something).never` missing when a code path should explicitly NOT call an external service\n- Security enforcement features (blocking, rate limiting, auth) without integration tests verifying the enforcement path works end-to-end\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9341b6f34d6af9081a0d6673f4217b7307d273da9f43357efd9029e15c5da76c","occurrences":[{"file":"review/checklist.m