is unrelated to the core purpose of importing browser cookies and expands the skill's side effects, increasing the chance of abuse, confusion, or persistence if the skill content is modified maliciously later.","remediation":"Remove contributor-report file creation from this skill and move it into a separate opt-in feedback skill or global trusted mechanism. If telemetry/reporting is required, make it explicit, narrowly scoped, user-consented, and disabled by default for security-sensitive workflows like cookie import.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"setup-browser-cookies/SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":79}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4729b48bb2fa4599ba3a783eeea8c3e7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"setup-browser-cookies/SKILL.md","start_line":83,"end_line":155},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill imports authenticated browser cookies into another browser session but does not present a prominent privacy and security warning before doing so. Because cookies can grant direct account access, users may underestimate the sensitivity of this action and expose production or personal sessions to unintended use within the automation environment.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning in the description and before execution that imported cookies may confer authenticated access and should only be used for intended test domains. Require explicit confirmation, encourage use of test accounts, and clearly explain persistence, scope, and how to clear imported cookies afterward.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"setup-browser-cookies/SKILL.md","start_line":83,"end_line":155}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3ee82ed047c54e6da47cf04ac6827e75","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":null},"finding":"create PR.\nallowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - Write\n  - Edit\n  - Grep\n  - Glob\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n<!-- AUTO-GENERATED from SKILL.md.tmpl — do not edit directly -->\n<!-- Regenerate: bun run gen:","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"name: ship\nversion: 1.0.0\ndescription: |\n  Ship workflow: detect + merge base branch, run tests, review diff, bump VERSION, update CHANGELOG, commit, push, create PR.\nallowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3011fe6f3214998b2b3c6487f9b609960af494aca42be848aa28606f96c22743","occurrences":[{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-e088041abd21415da1a6df918a590a94","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack","explanation":"The preamble creates and maintains per-process files under ~/.gstack/sessions and prunes them by age, which is a form of cross-run session/state persistence outside the repository. Persistent state can be used to track activity across sessions and may influence later behavior without clear user awareness or consent.","remediation":"Minimize persisted state and store it only when necessary with clear disclosure to the user. Use ephemeral temp storage where possible, document retention behavior, and provide an opt-out or cleanup command for session tracking files.","code_snippet":"```bash\n_UPD=$(~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || .claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-update-check 2>/dev/null || true)\n[ -n \"$_UPD\" ] && echo \"$_UPD\" || true\nmkdir -p ~/.gstack/sessions\ntouch ~/.gstack/sessions/\"$PPID\"\n_SESSIONS=$(find ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin -120 -type f 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nfind ~/.gstack/sessions -mmin +120 -type f -delete 2>/dev/null || true","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5e808e4c235a730213d17543b3ecd63b866e66e9ee00e0707fa038544ff15826","occurrences":[{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-317bf8f00be74728ae4322092109216a","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null},"finding":"write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n\n**ALWAYS follow this structure for every Ask","explanation":"The upgrade flow instructs the skill to read another skill file and write snooze state if the user declines an upgrade, introducing persistent user preference/state outside the immediate task. This hidden cross-session memory can affect future executions and is more concerning because it is embedded in an unrelated workflow.","remediation":"Disclose any persisted upgrade state to the user and require explicit consent before writing snooze preferences. Keep upgrade handling separate from task workflows, document storage location and retention, and allow users to inspect or clear stored state.","code_snippet":"echo \"BRANCH: $_BRANCH\"\n```\n\nIf output shows `UPGRADE_AVAILABLE <old> <new>`: read `~/.claude/skills/gstack/gstack-upgrade/SKILL.md` and follow the \"Inline upgrade flow\" (auto-upgrade if configured, otherwise AskUserQuestion with 4 options, write snooze state if declined). If `JUST_UPGRADED <from> <to>`: tell user \"Running gstack v{to} (just updated!)\" and continue.\n\n## AskUserQuestion Format\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"897ec9f9d58b2e14e9f5e1b059f4c1cef2b28ccbca8277d62d296f27bf766e10","occurrences":[{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a0486d9c538b4bacaed77aaf56aaf629","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":119},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow explicitly says it is non-interactive, should not ask for confirmation, and should always include uncommitted changes while proceeding through merge, test, commit, push, and PR creation. That creates a clear risk of shipping unintended local modifications or publishing changes the user did not realize would be included.","remediation":"Require an explicit pre-flight confirmation summarizing all pending actions, especially inclusion of uncommitted changes, branch merge, commit, push, and PR creation. Default to excluding unstaged/uncommitted work unless the user opts in, and add a dry-run mode that shows the exact files and commits before any remote action.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":119}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-afe34c93a7a94e3589b27a2299a03fcc","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":340,"end_line":null},"finding":"Do NOT ask the user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"   - Insert after the file header (line 5), dated today\n   - Format: `## [X.Y.Z.W] - YYYY-MM-DD`\n\n**Do NOT ask the user to describe changes.** Infer from the diff and commit history.\n\n---\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3e6d2470cd79db40290bf565b9000be6e8d6033acd7afb984d59587324307bd2","occurrences":[{"file":"ship/SKILL.md","start_line":340,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-0131cb81eac64b47b7f846b3bdf6dbd9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"test/helpers/llm-judge.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file explicitly requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and imports the Anthropic SDK, indicating dependency on third-party model access. Credentialed external AI-service access is not justified by the manifest's stated purpose of headless browser QA testing and therefore represents an additional capability outside the described context.","remediation":"Remove this helper from the skill runtime surface, or clearly declare the external AI-service dependency and its purpose in the skill's documentation and permissions model.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/helpers/llm-judge.ts","start_line":7,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-4f078dc077034e539384bb99efd6a4fb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"test/helpers/llm-judge.ts","start_line":32,"end_line":56},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a fast headless browser skill for QA testing and site dogfooding, but this helper transmits prompts, QA reports, and ground-truth bug data to Anthropic via `client.messages.create`. External LLM judging is not an obvious requirement of browser navigation, interaction, screenshotting, or page-state verification, so it adds a separate remote-evaluation capability beyond the stated purpose.","remediation":"Either document this external LLM-based evaluation capability explicitly in the skill description/test documentation, or isolate it outside the skill package so the browser skill remains limited to browser automation behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/helpers/llm-judge.ts","start_line":32,"end_line":56}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3c19c1bf7dc844699331d03ff4d3c41d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"test/helpers/session-runner.ts","start_line":145,"end_line":162},"finding":null,"explanation":"The subprocess is started with safety checks bypassed and no explicit disclosure or guardrails, so prompt-driven behavior can access tools under a more permissive trust model than a caller may expect. In this skill context, the helper is intended for automated E2E runs, which makes unattended misuse more plausible and amplifies the risk of prompt injection or unintended filesystem/process actions.","remediation":"Do not bypass permissions for the Claude subprocess. Add explicit safety documentation and runtime warnings for any elevated mode, require an opt-in flag for dangerous execution, and enforce least-privilege tool access plus sandboxing for automated tests.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/helpers/session-runner.ts","start_line":145,"end_line":162}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-75fcec78cd3c40388046442c936adc43","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"test/helpers/session-runner.ts","start_line":154,"end_line":156},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code writes the full prompt to `.prompt-tmp` in the working directory before execution, which can persist sensitive test data, secrets, or proprietary prompts on disk if cleanup fails or the directory is shared. In E2E environments, prompts often contain credentials, internal URLs, or reproduction details, so silent disk persistence increases exposure.","remediation":"Avoid writing prompts to disk when possible by piping them directly to the subprocess stdin. If a temp file is unavoidable, create it securely in an OS temp directory with restrictive permissions, use a unique filename, document the behavior, and ensure robust cleanup even on crashes/timeouts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/helpers/session-runner.ts","start_line":154,"end_line":156}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-622626a7292d48a8b1c3aee8d9608c59","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":127,"end_line":129},"finding":null,"explanation":"The test harness invokes `claude` with `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, explicitly bypassing the normal permission model for a subprocess. Even though this is framed as a connectivity smoke test, using a permission-bypass flag normalizes unsafe execution and could allow broader-than-intended command or file access if the invoked tool behavior changes or the environment is hostile.","remediation":"Remove `--dangerously-skip-permissions` from the connectivity check and use the least-privileged invocation possible. If a non-interactive check is required, gate it behind a dedicated test-only environment flag, document the risk clearly, and isolate the subprocess with a restricted environment and working directory.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":127,"end_line":129}]},{"id":"AS3","finding_id":"finding-d35