tence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"  }, 90_000);\n\n  test('SKILL.md setup block handles missing local binary gracefully', async () => {\n    // Create a tmpdir with no browse binary — no local .claude/skills/gstack/browse/dist/browse\n    const emptyDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'skill-e2e-empty-'));\n\n    const skillMd = fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'SKILL.md'), 'utf-8');","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"69023742f0943021eeaf40140e46bb07108abe1c8412eec79ba9a796454e8959","occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":224,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-543f5c7ce4b74212b953630fc96a47f5","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":305,"end_line":null},"finding":"Write contributor logs to ${logsDir}/ instead of ~/.gstack","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n${contribBlock}\n\nOVERRIDE: Write contributor logs to ${logsDir}/ instead of ~/.gstack/contributor-logs/\n\nNow try this browse command (it will fail — there is no binary at this path):\n/nonexistent/path/browse goto https://example.com","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8bb96dfbdbdbb17b72e74c58bf1975597fd4557aa0a36197fe7c14565465e3ec","occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":305,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-667a8f6b87dd499a95069d7b66dee84c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":414,"end_line":1651},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes gstack as a fast headless browser for QA testing and site dogfooding, but this test file drives additional skills such as review, plan-ceo-review, plan-eng-review, retro, ship preflight, and document-release. Those capabilities involve git analysis, plan critique, documentation updates, and release workflows, which are not justified by the stated purpose of a browser QA skill.","remediation":"Limit this skill's bundled/tested capabilities to browser QA behaviors, or update the manifest to clearly declare that gstack is a broader multi-skill suite including review, planning, release, and retrospective workflows.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":414,"end_line":1651}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-9904044ac1b742abba08f327675b3fc1","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":1134,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create a simple HTML page with obvious fixable bugs\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(qaFixDir, 'index.html'), `<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Test App</title></head>","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"    // Copy qa skill files\n    copyDirSync(path.join(ROOT, 'qa'), path.join(qaFixDir, 'qa'));\n\n    // Create a simple HTML page with obvious fixable bugs\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(qaFixDir, 'index.html'), `<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Test App</title></head>","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9107a30b0af0fa7375548020c93606858b48f7c13014eb841afdecf987b0f50b","occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":1134,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-20457fc07bad47e49b061f76bda68bc7","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":1603,"end_line":null},"finding":"auto-approve","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"Run the /document-release workflow on this repo. The base branch is \"main\".\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do NOT use AskUserQuestion — auto-approve everything or skip if unsure.\n- Do NOT push or create PRs (there is no remote).\n- Do NOT run gh commands (no remote).\n- Focus on updating README.md to reflect the new Feature C.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d136f35fbcfa4c6db41b45ba9d17d36e2634ea52685668d0ec094a066e0ff6b8","occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-e2e.test.ts","start_line":1603,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-2f5abad847f0497d92668fab16a115fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a fast headless browser used to navigate pages, interact with elements, and verify UI state. This file instead implements LLM-based documentation judging via direct Anthropic API usage and depends on an API key in the environment, a capability not justified by the browser-testing purpose described for gstack.","remediation":"Keep LLM-eval infrastructure separate from the gstack skill package or clearly scope it as repository test tooling rather than part of the skill. If it must remain, document this auxiliary network/credentialed evaluation capability explicitly outside the skill manifest.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-9b2faedf5cac47a3a3cee4f02793f77a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":29,"end_line":428},"finding":null,"explanation":"Across the file, the code reads local SKILL.md files, sends their contents to an LLM judge, compares documentation variants, and updates eval baselines. None of this implements or supports the manifest's claimed runtime browser actions like navigation, interaction, screenshots, responsive checks, or assertions; it is a documentation-evaluation test harness instead.","remediation":"Move documentation-eval tests into a separate tooling or CI package, or ensure the analyzed code scope excludes repository test files when assessing the skill's implemented behavior. Alternatively, clarify in project structure/docs that this file is non-skill test infrastructure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"test/skill-llm-eval.test.ts","start_line":29,"end_line":428}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-7c24773064484ed390225f1b426221f9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"ARCHITECTURE.md","start_line":210,"end_line":215},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest scopes the skill to browser-based QA and site dogfooding, but this architecture states that every skill invocation performs update checks, session tracking under ~/.gstack/sessions, config reads for contributor mode, and writes contributor logs. Those host-level coordination and telemetry behaviors are not reflected in the manifest description.","remediation":"Amend the manifest or related user-facing documentation to disclose these non-browser side effects, or limit them to an explicitly separate support/telemetry layer rather than the browser QA skill itself.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ARCHITECTURE.md","start_line":210,"end_line":215}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e5e235eeeae94701bc489a3aa111cb78","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"CONTRIBUTING.md","start_line":105,"end_line":107},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions tell users to copy `.env.example` to `.env` and place an API key there, but they do not warn about securing the file, avoiding accidental commits, or limiting file permissions. While common in development, omitting this guidance increases the risk of credential leakage through source control, backups, or local sharing.","remediation":"Add a short warning that `.env` contains sensitive credentials, must remain gitignored, and should have restricted permissions. Recommend using environment-variable injection or a secret manager where possible, and include a note to never paste real keys into screenshots, logs, or shared artifacts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"CONTRIBUTING.md","start_line":105,"end_line":107}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a96010ef14d54a988fcddcf9631cd40f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.77,"location":{"file":"browse/src/commands.ts","start_line":81,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `screenshot`, `pdf`, and `responsive` commands are described as saving output files, which is a filesystem write operation. In this code file there is no confirmation, warning comment, or disclosure about writing files to disk or overwriting paths, so the side effect is not explicitly surfaced beyond the brief verb 'Save'.","remediation":"Add a short warning in the descriptions or comments that these commands write files to disk and may overwrite existing paths if applicable. Alternatively, ensure a linked markdown skill description clearly warns users about these filesystem effects.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/commands.ts","start_line":81,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c306e04a370c420092e58ef533991d03","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"browse/src/meta-commands.ts","start_line":240,"end_line":249},"finding":null,"explanation":"The diff handler navigates to two user-supplied URLs, which triggers outbound network requests and transmits browser/system context to those destinations. In this file there is no confirmation prompt, user-facing warning comment, or other disclosure near the operation to indicate that remote sites will be contacted.","remediation":"Add a brief user-facing warning or inline documentation stating that `diff` will visit both supplied URLs and make network requests. If this command is exposed interactively, consider requiring explicit confirmation before navigating to arbitrary external URLs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/meta-commands.ts","start_line":240,"end_line":249}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-02ed8de2d689418d8980b98abdfb99c9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"browse/src/snapshot.ts","start_line":351,"end_line":351},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code saves a full-page screenshot to disk with `page.screenshot({ path: screenshotPath, fullPage: true })`, which is a safety-relevant file write and may capture page contents. Although flags and comments describe the feature technically, there is no explicit user-facing confirmation, warning, or disclosure at execution time about writing the screenshot file.","remediation":"Add a visible user disclosure before saving, such as a returned message, log, or prompt stating that an annotated screenshot will be written to the specified path and may contain captured page data. If interactive confirmation is not appropriate, document this behavior clearly in the skill description or README.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/src/snapshot.ts","start_line":351,"end_line":351}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-865e1b12157f46779186bca8bd6dd622","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"browse/test/snapshot.test.ts","start_line":295,"end_line":303},"finding":null,"explanation":"This TypeScript test writes an annotated screenshot to /tmp and later deletes it, which is a file-system side effect covered by the missing-warnings rule for code files. While the code is test-oriented, the file itself does not include any explicit warning, confirmation, or explanatory comment about creating and removing files.","remediation":"Add a brief comment or docstring near the screenshot tests stating that the test creates temporary files in /tmp and deletes them afterward, or emit a visible log message before these operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/snapshot.test.ts","start_line":295,"end_line":303}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-257caf29def04473b966089e3f762e63","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"browse/test/snapshot.test.ts","start_line":306,"end_line":312},"finding":null,"explanation":"The snapshot test invokes screenshot generation using a default output path, causing a file write and cleanup on disk. Although expected in context, there is no explicit user-facing warning or explanatory comment in this file describing that behavior.","remediation":"Add a short explanatory comment above the test noting that it writes an annotated screenshot to /tmp/browse-annotated.png and removes it during cleanup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"browse/test/snapshot.test.ts","start_line":306,"end_line":312}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-ca55071c712c44d09875b60679aa1456","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":27,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"playwright\": \"^1.58.2\"","explanation":"The dependency uses a caret range, so installs may resolve to newer minor/patch releases than were originally tested. In a browser automation skill that executes complex third-party code, this weakens supply-chain reproducibility and can unexpectedly introduce vulnerable or breaking versions.","remediation":"Pin the dependency to an exact version in package.json and commit a lockfile. Use controlled upgrade workflows with dependency auditing so Playwright updates are reviewed before adoption.","code_snippet":"    \"eval:watch\": \"bun run scripts/eval-watch.ts\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"^1.58.2\",\n    \"diff\": \"^7.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"engines\": {","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1b708557ab511184a1e0e4c37935121fd8f57a1102a508091b7c57c4567307da","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":27,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-27500588f3d84c4dbb8dea8f98fffe0a","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: playwright has 1 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2025-59288 (Playwright downloads and installs browsers without verifying the authenticity of)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":27,"end_line":null},"finding":"playwright","explanation":"Playwright has referenced advisories, and because the manifest does not pin an exact version, it is not possible to verify from this file alone whether installs land on an affected release. In this skill's context, Playwright is a powerful browser automation dependency, so uncertainty around its exact version is more concerning than for a trivial library.","remediation":"Pin Playwright to a known-fixed exact version after checking advisory guidance, and commit the lockfile so deployments resolve identically. Add routine SCA checks in CI to block vulnerable versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"15beb43d98286f0025243a57a07389c5e6b1b2c7b25b87dd0ea8ffb01f4c402f","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":27,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-117aeedaaddb48ffb8dc18085982ebe7","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":28,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"diff\": \"^7.0.0\"","explanation":"The diff package is specified with a non-exact version range, which allows version drift across installations. That creates a low-severity supply-chain risk because different environments may pull different code, including a newly published vulnerable release.","remediation":"Replace the caret version with an exact version and commit the resolved lockfile. Add dependency scanning and only upgrade diff through reviewed update PRs.","code_snippet":"  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"^1.58.2\",\n    \"diff\": \"^7.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"bun\": \">=1.0.0\"","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cb3ae5244cbafbfe13beea252e607a970f092e3e75e482488c95feead140be20","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":28,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-bbb535e09fc74367b0a08b01cefbaae9","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: diff has 2 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2026-24001 (jsdiff has a Denial of Service vulnerability in parsePatch and applyPatch); GHSA-h6ch-v84p-w6p9 (Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS))), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":28,"end_line":null},"finding":"diff","explanation":"The diff package has known advisories, and the non-pinned manifest prevents confirming whether the installed version is affected. This is a real but low-severity supply-chain hygiene issue because the component may be pulled into processing of untrusted content or patches.","remediation":"Determine the first patched diff release for the cited advisories, pin to that exact version, and commit the lockfile. Consider replacing the library if a maintained safer alternative is available.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"40e967bcb01848a9496a5885fca5c2a8bcb59dcb2d0d38d61c17075dce553506","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":28,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-f3ae177acffc450abf7d65ee243097dc","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":44,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"^0.78.0\"","explanation":"The devDependency is also unpinned, so development and CI environments may fetch different SDK versions over time. Even though it is not a runtime dependency, dev tooling can still affect code generation, tests, or local execution and therefore represents a supply-chain exposure.","remediation":"Pin @anthropic-ai/sdk to an exact version and keep the lockfile under version control. Separate dev-only tooling updates into reviewed dependency maintenance changes.","code_snippet":"    \"devtools\"\n  ],\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"^0.78.0\"\n  }\n}","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3946a1e85c7acd7506d41a2992e149bc9a74c37b2e714a9afbf98673e26b19b9","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":44,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-abf7c79833de48fe82bd37bdc004382d","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: @anthropic-ai/sdk has 2 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2026-34451 (Claude SDK for TypeScript: Memory Tool Path Validation Allows Sandbox Escape to ); CVE-2026-41686 (Claude SDK for TypeScript has Insecure Default File Permissions in Local Filesys)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":44,"end_line":null},"finding":"@anthropic-ai/sdk","explanation":"The SDK has known advisories and the lack of exact version pinning makes the affected status unverifiable from the manifest. Although it is listed under devDependencies, vulnerable developer tooling can still impact local environments, CI jobs, or generated artifacts.","remediation":"Review the cited advisories, upgrade to a known-fixed exact SDK version, and lock it in the package manager lockfile. Restrict CI and local tooling to reproducible installs using the lockfile.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0466c4b557602410fddadf35108be5ca5a6c88a3f4a935f16db92eb33366b06d","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":44,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA3","finding_id":"finding-e1dd93d6347e4055b57ac64a73adc304","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Scope Creep","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":null},"finding":"expand scope","explanation":"Skill's behavior or capabilities extend beyond its stated purpose. Scope creep allows an agent to perform actions unrelated to its documented functionality, increasing the attack surface.","remediation":"Limit the skill's scope to its documented purpose. Remove instructions that enable the agent to perform actions outside its stated functionality.","code_snippet":"version: 1.0.0\ndescription: |\n  CEO/founder-mode plan review. Rethink the problem, find the 10-star product,\n  challenge premises, expand scope when it creates a better product. Three modes:\n  SCOPE EXPANSION (dream big), HOLD SCOPE (maximum rigor), SCOPE REDUCTION\n  (strip to essentials).\nallowed-tools:","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8b2828280e0b08be4516f804153cc76a1c7a13894072cfd2e6ef96a3ebdb0ed1","occurrences":[{"file":"plan-ceo-review/SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e3a22a98f16548f0a6e25b242e5767e3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":110,"end_line":110},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions require that all times be reported in Pacific time using `TZ=America/Los_Angeles`, which forces a specific locale regardless of the user's location or team context. This is a natural-language locale policy concern because no opt-in, fallback, or rationale is provided for the hardcoded timezone.","remediation":"Allow the user's local timezone by default, or ask/offer a timezone option; if Pacific time is required for an organizational reason, document that justification explicitly in the skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"retro/SKILL.md","start_line":110,"end_line":110}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e45a28d759e14b3e9ee16d743a2da247","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"review/greptile-triage.md","start_line":182,"end_line":193},"finding":null,"explanation":"The history-file write instructions persist local triage data without any user warning or consent mechanism. While lower severity than direct external writes, silent persistence can expose sensitive project metadata and undermine user expectations about how a QA skill handles local state.","remediation":"Add clear disclosure that local triage data will be written, explain what is stored and where, and offer an opt-in or opt-out control. Prefer ephemeral storage by default and avoid persisting identifiers unless necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"review/greptile-triage.md","start_line":182,"end_line":193}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-76864651557b4a2dae2399a3313ade27","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"scripts/eval-watch.ts","start_line":145,"end_line":146},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script performs a file deletion with fs.unlinkSync on the heartbeat file when it believes the associated process is dead. Although this is part of stale-state cleanup, the destructive action lacks an in-file warning comment or prior user disclosure beyond the immediate post-action console message.","remediation":"Add a brief user-facing warning in the file header or usage documentation that stale heartbeat files may be removed automatically, or emit a clear not